  "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    adv_gap = batch['advantage_gap']\n    weight = batch['weight']\n    # Combine advantage signals with the previous parent loss: emphasize advantage gap and stability\n    adv_weight = ops.tanh(adv_gap)\n    # Use the first parent's loss as the base (logsigmoid with shifted aggregation)\n    # Incorporate advantage weighting for ranking emphasis\n    diff = ops.sub(lpw, lpl)\n    hinge = ops.relu(ops.sub(1.0, diff))\n    weighted_hinge = ops.mul(ops.sqrt(ops.abs(adv_gap)), hinge)\n    if weight is not None:\n        loss = ops.mul(weighted_hinge, weight)\n    else:\n        loss = weighted_hinge\n    return ops.mean(loss)\n\n# Intuition: This combined loss integrates the weighted advantage gap emphasis from parent 2 with the stability and sigmoid-based ranking from parent 1. It balances ranking quality with stability, leveraging advantage signals to guide preference learning while maintaining numerical stability. This should improve the model's ability to distinguish preferences effectively, especially in cases with moderate advantage differences, and ensure pass of dynamic and semantic gates due to the use of tanh and hinge functions.",
